# Decision-oriented UX

Optimize for the named persona finishing a specified flow, not for a landing page.

- Lead with decision verbs (escalate, review, acknowledge, flag, confirm — whatever the flow needs).
- The first screen must answer the primary decision in one scan (rank, filters, or equivalent).
- Two clicks from a “needs attention” row to *why*.
- Implement empty states when a domain or list has no items.
- Desktop-first (1280+), dense tables and KPI strips. Do not add illustration-heavy chrome.
- Session-only controls must say they do not persist.
